    text: "---"
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "scene 017.2 — nibiru's shadow: engineered winter"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "scene meta:"
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "location: Sol-3 Surface (Northern Landmass)"
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "time: year 14,000"
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "participants: Zephyr, scattered Igigi refugees, indigenous surface populations"
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "focus: Zephyr emerges from his shelter on Sol-3 to witness Nibiru sliding between Sol-3 and its star, casting an engineered perpetual shadow that plunges the planet into grinding cold and disrupts surface populations and refugee survival."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "continuity: Immediately follows the Anunnaki orbital deployment in scene 017.1"
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "presentation: cutscene"
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "cutscene purpose: The visual and environmental onset of Nibiru's shadow and perpetual ice age over Sol-3."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "Sol-3 Surface - Northern Landmass"
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "Zephyr felt the change before he saw it—a disturbance in the mathematical harmonics of local space-time that made his consciousness recoil from the quantum calculations he'd been attempting."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "Around the crude shelter he'd constructed from indigenous materials, the temperature had been dropping steadily for cycles, but this felt different."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "Purposeful."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "He emerged from the shelter and looked up at the sky, his enhanced Igigi vision perceiving electromagnetic spectra far beyond the range of the primitive indigenous species."
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "What he saw made his mathematical mind stagger with the implications."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "A dark world, vast beyond comprehension, sliding between the local star and the planet surface like a predator moving to devour its prey."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "The shadow it cast wasn't merely the absence of light—it was the presence of cold, engineered and deliberate, designed to persist."
  - line: 41
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"Nibiru,\""
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "Across the continents, he could sense the other scattered refugees discovering the same horror."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "The Anunnaki hadn't pursued them across the void to kill them quickly and cleanly."
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "Instead, they had brought winter itself, transformed it into a weapon of slow execution."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "The indigenous populations—primitive bipedal mammals with crude stone-age technologies—were already beginning to suffer."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "Their agricultural systems, barely above subsistence level, started failing as crops froze in fields that had never known winter."
  - line: 49
    type: narration
    text: "Their settlements, designed for temperate climates, offered no protection against the grinding cold that Nibiru's shadow brought."
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "But it was the refugees who would suffer most."
  - line: 52
    type: narration
    text: "The Igigi, scattered and alone, watching the world they'd chosen for sanctuary transform into a frozen wasteland that would make their survival a daily struggle against entropy itself."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "Zephyr's mathematical consciousness began processing survival calculations, but for the first time in his existence, the numbers offered no comfort."
  - line: 55
    type: narration
    text: "Food production would cease within local cycles."
  - line: 56
    type: narration
    text: "Energy requirements for basic thermal maintenance would exhaust their consciousness-reserves within a standard year."
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "The indigenous biosphere would collapse, eliminating any possibility of integration or symbiosis."
  - line: 59
    type: narration
    text: "They had traded the quick death of honorable battle for the slow extinction of starvation and cold."
  - line: 61
    type: narration
    text: "As the first storm winds began to howl across the darkening landscape, carrying ice that cut like blades of glass, Zephyr felt the weight of their choice settling around him like chains."
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "The Anunnaki had given them exactly what they'd asked for—survival."
  - line: 63
    type: narration
    text: "Just enough of it to make them regret the asking."
  - line: 65
    type: narration
    text: "The punishment had begun."
  - line: 67
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 69
    type: narration
    text: "approximately Year 14,014"

